---
description: Write em-dash-free prose and avoid the sentence shapes that invite an em dash
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the writing rules in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repository root.

In short: never use an em dash (U+2014) or its stand-ins (a double hyphen, a spaced
hyphen, a stray en dash, the horizontal bar) as sentence punctuation. Replace them with
commas, semicolons, colons, periods, or parentheses, and recast when a plain swap reads
awkwardly. Keep ordinary hyphens in compounds, ranges, code, and Markdown structure.
See `AGENTS.md` for the full playbook.
